<title>USA: Duke Catawba S.C. nuke at 60 pct and rising.</title>
<headline>Duke Catawba S.C. nuke at 60 pct and rising.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Duke Power Co's 1,129 megawatt Catawba 2 nuclear power unit was operating at 60 percent power early Monday due to a condenser tube leak, the Nuclear Regulatory Commission (NRC) said in its status report.</p>
<p>Repairs have been completed, and the unit will likely return to full power sometime this morning, the NRC report stated.</p>
<p>The adjacent unit 1, with an identical generating capacity, is operating at 100 percent of capacity.</p>
<p>Both units are located in Clover, S.C.</p>
<p>((--New York Power Desk +212-859-1628))</p>
